cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SatQuery AI, its fine-tuning methodology, or its empirical coordinate calibration in your research, please cite this work."
title: "SatQuery: An Edge-Deployable Agentic Vision-Language Architecture for Grounded Remote Sensing Perception and Multi-Sensory Reasoning"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kazi
    given-names: Sameel
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Engineering, Sardar Patel Institute of Technology (SPIT), Mumbai"
    email: "sameel.kazi@spit.ac.in"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3925-976X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sameelkazi/satquery"
url: "https://github.com/sameelkazi/satquery"
abstract: >-
  SatQuery is an integrated, edge-deployable multimodal architecture for
  grounded remote-sensing perception, combining parameter-efficient
  vision-language grounding (LoRA-adapted Qwen2.5-VL / Qwen3-VL on
  VRSBench), bi-temporal change detection, optical-SAR cross-modal fusion,
  and zero-shot land-cover classification behind an agentic semantic
  intent router.
